    "description": "# Future Directions\n\nThis cycle deepened the \"Graph Coloring with Emotions\" thread from a qualitative invariant\n(`emoChrom`, the emotional chromatic number) to a **quantitative closed form**: the full chromatic\npolynomial of the friendship (windmill) graph.\n\n## What was proved (`Catalog/Novelty/FriendshipChromaticPolynomial.lean`)\n\n- `chromVal_friendship` : `P(F_n, q) = q \u00b7 ((q-1)(q-2))^n` for all `n, q`, via an explicit bijection\n  (`frEquiv`) between proper colourings and (centre colour) \u00d7 (per-triangle admissible pair), whose\n  fibre count `(q-1)(q-2)` is established in `pairColors_card`.\n- `friendship_chromVal_six` : `P(F_n, 6) = 6 \u00b7 20^n` \u2014 the original conjecture (six basic emotions).\n- `chromVal_pos_iff_colorable`, `friendship_colorable_three`, `friendship_colorable_six`,\n  `friendship_not_colorable_two`, `friendship_chromaticNumber` (`\u03c7(F_n) = 3` for `n \u2265 1`).\n\n## Also proved (`Catalog/Novelty/FriendshipEmotionalChromaticNumber.lean`)\n\nThe bridge to the emotional-chromatic-number invariant (former next step 6, now **done**):\n\n- `emoChrom_friendship` : `emoChrom (F_n) = 3` for every `n`, obtained by feeding\n  `friendship_colorable_three` into `emoChrom_eq_three_iff`.\n- `emoChrom_friendship_within_window` : `3 \u2264 emoChrom (F_n) \u2264 6` \u2014 every friendship network sits\n  inside the six-basic-emotions window.\n- `chromVal_emoChrom_friendship` : `P(F_n, emoChrom (F_n)) = 3 \u00b7 2^n`.\n- `emoChrom_eq_chromaticNumber_friendship` : for `n \u2265 1`, `emoChrom (F_n) = \u03c7(F_n)` (both `3`).\n\n## Natural next steps\n\n1. **Generalized windmills `Wd(m, n)`** (`n` copies of `K_m` glued at a vertex): the same bijection\n   generalizes to `P = q \u00b7 (q-1)^{\\underline{m-1}}{}^{\\,n}` where `(q-1)^{\\underline{m-1}}` is the\n   falling factorial `(q-1)(q-2)\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7(q-m+1)`. The friendship graph is the `m = 3` case.\n2. **Book graphs / fans / gear graphs**: other one-common-vertex gluings with clean product forms.\n3. **Deletion\u2013contraction cross-check**: rederive `chromVal_friendship` from the recurrence in\n   `Catalog/Combinatorics/ChromaticPolynomial.lean` (deleting/contracting one triangle edge) and\n   prove the two derivations agree, tightening the bridge between the counting and algebraic views.\n4. **Polynomiality and roots**: lift `chromVal` to a genuine `Polynomial \u2124` and show its integer\n   roots are exactly `{0, 1, 2}`, matching the emotional floor `emoChrom = 3`.\n5. **Coefficient combinatorics**: expand `q\u00b7((q-1)(q-2))^n` and connect the alternating-sign\n   coefficients to Whitney's broken-circuit theorem for this graph family.\n6. **Bridge to `emoChrom`** \u2014 *done*, see `Catalog/Novelty/FriendshipEmotionalChromaticNumber.lean`\n   (`emoChrom_friendship : emoChrom (F_n) = 3`, extended to the whole family, plus the\n   window and chromatic-number consequences).\n",
