    "description": "# Future directions\n\nThis cycle deepened the study of the **square of the Eulerian triangle**, whose `n`-th row\npolynomial is `B_n(x) = \u2211_k (\u2211_j A(n,j)\u00b7A(j,k)) x^k`.\n\n## What was proved (`Catalog/Cryptography/EulerianSquareDeepening.lean`)\n\n1. **Structural identity** `sqPoly_eq_sum_eulPoly`:\n   `B_n(x) = \u2211_j A(n,j)\u00b7A_j(x)`, exhibiting `B_n` as a nonnegative combination of the\n   Eulerian polynomials `A_j`.\n2. **General negativity of roots** `sqPoly_root_neg` (all `n`, unconditional): every real\n   root of `B_n` is strictly negative, via positivity `sqPoly_eval_pos_of_nonneg`\n   (`B_n(x) > 0` for `x \u2265 0`).\n3. **Extension past the boundary** `eulerianSquare_realRooted`: `B_n` is real-rooted for\n   every `n \u2264 10` (previous work reached `n \u2264 7`), breaking the integer-bracket obstruction\n   at `n = 8` with rational brackets; and the strengthened `eulerianSquare_realRooted_neg`\n   (splits with all roots real and negative for `n \u2264 10`).\n\n## Open problems and natural next steps\n\n* **The full conjecture.**  Prove `RealRooted (sqPoly n)` for *every* `n`.  The identity\n  `B_n = \u2211_j A(n,j)\u00b7A_j` reduces this to showing that the family `(A_0, \u2026, A_n)` of Eulerian\n  polynomials is **compatible** (every nonnegative combination is real-rooted), which for a\n  sequence generated by a recurrence follows from **mutual interlacing**.  Formalizing\n  interlacing preservation under the Eulerian recurrence operator is the key missing piece.\n\n* **Interlacing infrastructure in Lean.**  Mathlib currently lacks a general theory of\n  interlacing / compatible polynomials and the Hermite\u2013Biehler-type stability results.\n  Building this (definition of interlacing via sign patterns at roots, the \"common\n  interlacer\" lemma, closure of compatibility under nonnegative combinations) would unlock\n  not only the Eulerian-square conjecture but real-rootedness preservation for squares of\n  the Pascal, Stirling and Narayana triangles as well.\n\n* **Higher powers.**  Extend from the *square* to arbitrary powers `T^m` of the Eulerian\n  triangle: is the `n`-th row of `T^m` real-rooted for all `m, n`?  The identity generalizes\n  to `B^{(m)}_n = \u2211_j A(n,j)\u00b7B^{(m-1)}_j`, suggesting an induction on `m` once compatibility\n  is available.\n\n* **Uniform bracket family.**  A more elementary (bracket-only) route to all `n` would need\n  a uniform family of rational separating brackets; none is currently known, since the\n  smallest roots cluster toward `0` as `n` grows (see `ComputationalEvidence.md`).\n\n* **Coefficient structure.**  Prove in general that `B_n` is monic of degree `n-2` with all\n  positive coefficients and constant term `n!` (only `1 \u2264 C(n,0)` is used here); this would\n  also give clean degree/leading-coefficient lemmas for the induction above.\n",
