    "description": "# Future Directions\n\nTwo self-contained Lean files (each importing only Mathlib) realize the mission\n\"Paradoxes as Theorems: Liar, Berry, and Russell Made Consistent\":\n\n- `Catalog/Logic/ParadoxesConsistentConnector.lean` establishes a bridge\n  between Boolean-algebra theory and the metatheory of self-referential\n  paradoxes:\n  - A negation fixed point in any Boolean algebra collapses it (`\u22a5 = \u22a4`), so a\n    consistent theory with a Liar-style sentence cannot be Boolean-valued.\n  - Belnap's four-valued logic `BV` supplies a *designated* negation fixed point\n    `B`, and an explicit six-sentence paraconsistent theory makes the Liar,\n    Russell and Berry sentences simultaneously provable while staying nontrivial\n    and non-explosive.\n- `Catalog/Logic/ParadoxSelfSoundness.lean` gives a fully computational finite\n  certificate: it develops a small paraconsistent-logic vocabulary (Belnap\n  values, a paraconsistent theory, soundness, explosion, inconsistency degree)\n  and verifies, by decision procedure, that the concrete six-element model has\n  three distinct provable gluts, is self-sound, rejects explosion, and has\n  inconsistency degree exactly three.\n\nNatural continuations:\n\n1. **Full propositional paraconsistent calculus.** Extend `ParaTheory` with a\n   syntax of connectives (`\u2227, \u2228, \u00ac, \u2192`) interpreted through `conj`, `disj`,\n   `neg`, and prove a soundness/completeness theorem for the designated-value\n   consequence relation `\u0393 \u22a8 \u03c6`.\n\n2. **Algebraic generality.** Replace `BV` by an arbitrary De Morgan bilattice\n   and characterize exactly which finite De Morgan algebras admit a designated\n   negation fixed point (equivalently, host a consistent Liar). Relate this to\n   the failure of the law of non-contradiction / excluded middle.\n\n3. **Encoding genuine self-reference.** Connect the abstract fixed-point value\n   `B` to a real diagonalization: a G\u00f6del-style fixed-point lemma producing a\n   sentence provably equivalent to its own negation inside a paraconsistent\n   arithmetic, so that \"Liar/Russell/Berry\" are derived rather than posited.\n\n4. **Berry-specific refinement.** Model definability/nameability bounds so that\n   Berry's paradox arises from an explicit least-undefinable-number construction\n   rather than sharing the generic self-negation shape.\n\n5. **Quantitative inconsistency.** Study the \"inconsistency degree\" (number of\n   gluts) as an invariant of paraconsistent theories and its behaviour under\n   theory extensions and morphisms.\n",
